WPE: allow turning off process swap on navigation

WPE always swaps web processes on cross-site navigation (and for COOP); GTK has the
process-swap-on-cross-site-navigation-enabled property for it. The webOS browser's direct
presentation gives each web process its own compositor surface for a view, and the webOS
compositor cannot hand the view's layer from one process's surface to another's without
hiding the app. WPE_BROWSER_NO_PROCESS_SWAP (set by the engine in that mode) keeps a view in its process.

--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/glib/WebKitWebContext.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/glib/WebKitWebContext.cpp
@@ -448,7 +448,10 @@
     configuration.setUseSystemAppearanceForScrollbars(priv->useSystemAppearanceForScrollbars);
 #endif
 #else
-    configuration.setProcessSwapsOnNavigation(true);
+    // webOS browser: WPE_BROWSER_NO_PROCESS_SWAP keeps a view in its web process on cross-site navigation (and COOP).
+    // Direct presentation gives each web process its own compositor surface for the view, and the webOS compositor
+    // cannot move the view's layer from one process's surface to another's without hiding the app.
+    configuration.setProcessSwapsOnNavigation(!g_getenv("WPE_BROWSER_NO_PROCESS_SWAP"));
 #endif
     if (priv->memoryPressureSettings) {
         configuration.setMemoryPressureHandlerConfiguration(webkitMemoryPressureSettingsGetMemoryPressureHandlerConfiguration(priv->memoryPressureSettings));
